WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.180
Marvel fans have long adored Chris Evans'
take on the iconic superhero Captain America.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:10.050
But now he's at the end of the line with his
movie contract, what does that actually mean

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.420
for the MCU?

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:15.490
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'll be explaining what the events

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.650
of Endgame mean for the future of Captain
America, the real reason behind Cap's choice

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.210
in the movie, and why we may get a Steve Rogers
spin-off.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:26.920
My Marvel giveaway is still running, so subscribe
and leave a comment about Captain America

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.300
for a chance to win.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.150
Spoilers ahead if you haven't seen the movie
yet.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:35.800
At the end of Endgame, Steve Rogers goes on
one final mission: to place the Infinity Stones

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.079
back in their original locations.

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:42.829
Steve returns, but not quite as expected,
and we discover he's made two major decisions

00:00:42.829 --> 00:00:44.949
that will alter the future of the MCU.

00:00:44.949 --> 00:00:49.230
First during his trip to the past, he married
his long-lost love Peggy Carter.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:53.699
And then he returned as Old Man Steve, bringing
with him a new Captain America shield which

00:00:53.699 --> 00:00:55.489
he gave to Sam Wilson.

00:00:55.489 --> 00:00:59.699
Sam accepts the shield, signalling that he'll
become the new Captain America.

00:00:59.699 --> 00:01:03.570
This decision has left some fans surprised
as they were expecting Bucky to be Steve's

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:07.680
successor as he's been around longer than
Falcon in the MCU, and the friendship between

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.600
Steve and Bucky has been given particular
prominence in the Captain America movies.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.570
"I can get by on my own.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.030
I'm with you to the end of the line, pal."

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.040
"I'm not gonna fight you.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.040
You're my friend.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.040
You're my mission!

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.040
Then finish it.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.520
Because I'm with you to the end of the line."

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.350
In fact, before Steve leaves the current timeline
to return the Infinity Stones, he has a heartfelt

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:29.340
goodbye with Bucky whose words 'I'm gonna
miss you, buddy' show that he knows Steve

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.640
isn't going to come back the same man as he
left.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:37.240
Steve also tells Bucky not to do anything
stupid until he gets back and Bucky replies

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.240
"How can I?

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:42.530
You're taking all the stupid with you", which
is a sweet call-back to this moment in Cap's

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:45.030
first movie when Bucky left Steve to go to
war.

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:47.140
"Don't do anything stupid until I get back.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.140
How can I?

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.360
You're taking all the stupid with you."

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.590
Like Sam, Bucky has been Captain America in
the comics, and given how the passing of the

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:58.270
shield from Steve to Bucky has been foreshadowed
many times in the MCU, some fans have been

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:01.170
upset that Steve didn't give him the shield
in the end.

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:05.130
Now, Bucky may still become Captain America
in the future, but there are several good

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:08.950
reasons why now isn't necessarily the right
time for him.

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:12.810
First of all, we need to remember that Bucky
was only recently rehabilitated when he was

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:16.870
taken to Wakanda at the end of Civil War to
have the HYDRA programming removed from his

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:17.870
brain.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.820
This was successful, but Bucky still had to
wait through a recovery period during which

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.160
he became the White Wolf in Wakanda.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:28.750
And although he fought alongside the Avengers
in Infinity War, Bucky may not be ready yet

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.380
for something like becoming Captain America.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:35.680
In fact, during Civil War, Bucky reveals the
doubts he has about himself to Steve:

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.670
"I don't know if I'm worth all this, Steve.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:38.670
What you did all those years...

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:39.670
It wasn't you.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:40.670
You didn't have a choice.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:41.760
I know.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.120
But I did it."

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.120
And there is the problem.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.990
Before the events of Infinity War and Endgame,
Bucky was a wanted assassin and even if his

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:53.440
crimes have been forgiven after he stood with
the Avengers against Thanos, the powers-that-be,

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.830
for example, Thunderbolt Ross might try and
stand in the way of someone with such a troubled

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:00.470
history taking up the mantle of Captain America.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:05.720
Especially given that Bucky killed Tony Stark's
parents; after all, it was Tony's father Howard

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.870
who created the original Captain America shield.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:12.500
Perhaps more importantly though, there's a
good chance that Steve just doesn't want to

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.819
place the weight and responsibility of being
Captain America on Bucky's shoulders at this

00:03:16.819 --> 00:03:20.290
point in time given all his friend has been
through.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:24.880
In any case, Bucky seems at ease with how
Steve left him at the end of Avengers: Endgame.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:29.440
And it's quite possible that Bucky had a conversation
with Steve off-screen before he left to travel

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:30.440
back in time.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:34.670
Indeed, the Russos have confirmed that when
the pair say goodbye to each other and Bucky

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.380
"says I'll miss you.'

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.090
Clearly [Bucky] knows something."

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:42.970
Cap and Bucky's possible off-screen conversation
could explain why Bucky tells Sam to "go ahead"

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:45.700
and talk to Steve after he returns from the
past.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:50.470
In fact, after Steve tells Sam to try on the
shield, Sam looks back to Bucky as if to check

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:55.599
with him, and Bucky nods back in approval,
as if he already knew this moment was coming.

00:03:55.599 --> 00:04:00.281
So, when Sam accepts the shield and says he'll
do his best and Steve replies "that's why

00:04:00.281 --> 00:04:04.860
it's yours", it's a subtle indication that
Sam has the right mind-set to become the new

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.220
Captain America.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:10.820
The passing of the mantle from Steve to Sam
was cleverly foreshadowed several times during

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:11.820
Endgame.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:15.260
When Steve is acting as a counsellor to help
people work through how they feel about the

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:20.729
world after Thanos's snap, it parallels nicely
with Sam's work as a PTSD counsellor for veterans

00:04:20.729 --> 00:04:22.210
in The Winter Soldier film.

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:27.330
Then later, as Cap was about to make his solo
last stand against Thanos, he hears Sam's

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:31.599
voice through his earpiece saying 'on your
left', as all the dusted heroes return for

00:04:31.599 --> 00:04:34.379
that epic Avengers Assemble moment.

00:04:34.379 --> 00:04:38.879
Sam's "on your left" is a lovely hat-tip to
Steve's first words to him in The Winter Soldier

00:04:38.879 --> 00:04:43.439
movie, and again, foreshadows how Steve and
Sam will later swap roles at the close of

00:04:43.439 --> 00:04:44.439
Endgame.

00:04:44.439 --> 00:04:49.439
Likewise, there's more to Cap and Sam's final
conversation than first meets the eye.

00:04:49.439 --> 00:04:54.210
When Steve tells Sam to try on the shield,
then asks him how it feels, Sam says, "Like

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.599
it's someone else's."

00:04:55.599 --> 00:05:00.749
Steve's reply that "it isn't" not only confirms
that he sees Sam as the new Captain, but it's

00:05:00.749 --> 00:05:05.689
also a reminder that this isn't Steve's original
shield, because that one was broken when Thanos

00:05:05.689 --> 00:05:08.219
smashed it during the final battle in Endgame.

00:05:08.219 --> 00:05:12.289
This new shield would seem to be one that
Steve has brought to Sam from the alternate

00:05:12.289 --> 00:05:15.629
reality that he lived in when he went back
to live with Peggy.

00:05:15.629 --> 00:05:19.819
When Steve decided to return to the present
timeline, he knew that a Captain America shield

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:21.120
didn't exist any longer.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:26.289
So, it's possible that in his alternate reality,
Steve asked Peggy, Howard Stark or even Tony

00:05:26.289 --> 00:05:28.669
to get him a shield for Sam.

00:05:28.669 --> 00:05:32.719
Another possibility is that there was a Falcon
who was Captain America in Steve's alternate

00:05:32.719 --> 00:05:37.979
reality and now Steve is bringing our present-day
Sam that other Falcon's shield.

00:05:37.979 --> 00:05:42.669
Falcon adopting Cap's title also nods back
to the comics, where it's happened a few times.

00:05:42.669 --> 00:05:47.879
The most interesting example that relates
to Avengers: Endgame is from 2014 when Steve

00:05:47.879 --> 00:05:51.909
passed on the shield to Sam after he'd lost
his super-soldier powers and turned into an

00:05:51.909 --> 00:05:53.089
old man.

00:05:53.089 --> 00:05:57.900
So, what does Sam taking the Captain America
shield mean for Anthony Mackie and Sebastian

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.490
Stan's new TV show on Disney+?

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:03.939
Well, as their series is called Falcon And
Winter Soldier, it seems like Sam might need

00:06:03.939 --> 00:06:09.159
a little while to work himself up to being
Captain America and all that the title entails.

00:06:09.159 --> 00:06:13.349
Likewise, that would also give fans time to
adjust to a new actor stepping into Chris

00:06:13.349 --> 00:06:14.479
Evans's super-shoes.

00:06:14.479 --> 00:06:18.619
As for Bucky fans, they may still see the
Winter Soldier pick up the shield at some

00:06:18.619 --> 00:06:20.469
point during the show[, and possibly even
share the role with Sam].

00:06:20.469 --> 00:06:25.659
After all, Sebastian Stan did tell fans back
in 2016 at Nerdist's Civil War movie marathon

00:06:25.659 --> 00:06:30.539
that Marvel had told him that "eventually
[Bucky was] gonna become Captain America".

00:06:30.539 --> 00:06:34.460
Another interesting possibility that the introduction
of alternate timelines has brought to the

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:39.439
MCU is that, although Steve Rogers' story
in Endgame did wrap up his character arc nicely,

00:06:39.439 --> 00:06:43.599
there's still potential for future films or
TV shows about Steve and Peggy's alternate

00:06:43.599 --> 00:06:44.740
life together.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:49.249
In fact, the Russos have confirmed that when
Steve went back in time he created "a branched

00:06:49.249 --> 00:06:53.189
reality" and they said there's a possible
story to be told about what Steve did in that

00:06:53.189 --> 00:06:57.009
reality and how he ended up coming back to
give the shield to Falcon.

00:06:57.009 --> 00:07:01.499
I'm sure many would love to see a Steve Rogers
and Peggy Carter movie, but right now Chris

00:07:01.499 --> 00:07:05.430
Evans's contract has ended and he's doubtless
looking forward to playing a wider variety

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:06.999
of roles going forward.

00:07:06.999 --> 00:07:11.430
He's also talked about wanting to leave the
MCU on a high, or to use his own words, 'You

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.899
want to get off the train before they push
you off'.

00:07:13.899 --> 00:07:18.009
Still, it's possible Evans might entertain
coming back at some point in the future and

00:07:18.009 --> 00:07:21.759
maybe the upcoming Disney+ shows could be
something he'd consider.

00:07:21.759 --> 00:07:25.879
For example, one of the new Marvel shows is
an animated "What If?" series and the very

00:07:25.879 --> 00:07:29.819
first episode will explore what would have
happened if Peggy Carter had been given the

00:07:29.819 --> 00:07:34.659
Super-Soldier Serum in place of Steve who,
instead, will eventually join World War 2

00:07:34.659 --> 00:07:36.749
using a metal suit created by Howard Stark.

00:07:36.749 --> 00:07:40.990
According to reports, the "What If?" series
will feature the voices of actors from the

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:41.990
MCU movies.

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:45.719
So, hopefully, at the very least, we'll get
to hear Hayley Atwell and Chris Evans as the

00:07:45.719 --> 00:07:48.240
voices of Peggy and Steve in that show.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:51.529
As for the longer term, well, there's plenty
of actors who've eventually gone back to roles

00:07:51.529 --> 00:07:53.969
that they thought they'd left way in their
past.

00:07:53.969 --> 00:07:55.330
So, never say never!

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:58.210
So, how do you feel about Falcon becoming
Captain America?

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:02.129
And would you like to see Chris Evans return
to the MCU?

